{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "T21-2d: the inferred array witness crosses a forwarding-only `var` parameter (place's rows reaches set_row and is_free), so the callee's stores lower on the typed lane (raw byte store with the CW32 cold arm array_num_set_cow_idx) instead of index_assign_cow/fn_array_set, and a store whose key is a parameter used only as an indexed-store subscript still gets the int lane (the key of `rows[r] = v` is numeric use). The guarded store of an untyped value must NOT take the declared-contract checked store: an untyped pn parameter's implicit contract is `any \\ error`, which lambda_array_set_checked_inplace rejects for every element (E201), and the callee then left through the error lane before writing -- queens' set_row_column lost every write that way. widen's string store pins that the representation-agnostic arm still widens the packed lane in place.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_set_row_#",
      "expect": [
        "i64:_array_witness",
        "call\tarray_num_set_cow_idx_p, array_num_set_cow_idx"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        "call\tlambda_array_set_checked_inplace_p, lambda_array_set_checked_inplace",
        "call\tindex_assign_cow_p, index_assign_cow",
        "call\tfn_array_set_p, fn_array_set"
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_place_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tfn_index_p, fn_index",
        "call\titem_at_p, item_at",
        "call\tfn_array_set_p, fn_array_set",
        "call\tindex_assign_cow_p, index_assign_cow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_widen_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tlambda_array_set_checked_inplace_p, lambda_array_set_checked_inplace",
        "call\tindex_assign_cow_p, index_assign_cow"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
